[ ] Media stack\: Usenet and torrents into a media dir, served by Jellyfin =media-stack $Darrion's vision, 2026-10-24: an alternative to the streaming services. Newshosting (the Usenet provider) plus nzbget fetch from Usenet, a torrent client adds the rest, both write into one media directory on this machine's storage, and Jellyfin serves it. nzbget runs on the desktop for now while Darrion learns it; the downloaders belong here, since the desktop sleeps. Notes for when it starts: the hardware may be an old ThinkStation instead of the N150 (Darrion, not decided); media is re-downloadable, so the RAID1 mirror is enough and it stays out of the B2 and Drive backups; the torrent client should only reach the network through a VPN, since a swarm sees its IP; nzbget's default web login must change. Start minimal (no Sonarr or Radarr until manual use shows the need). Ethics, open (2026-10-24): Darrion pays for media and wants higher-quality copies that are theirs to keep, and is unsure how to do that ethically, which is why this has never been top priority. Discussed, cleanest first: rip owned discs (UHD Blu-ray beats streams; MakeMKV), DRM-free purchases, copies of things already bought, then unpaid downloads (not wanted). Candidate rule, not adopted: only keep what I've paid for. Not a priority now.$ !4 ^2026-10-24T21:59 <services-up #01a16fed-079c-7470-bf80-5a5637773114
