    >[-] Services image\: operator access, key-only SSH and Tailscale, booted in a VM =services-access $First increment of =services-up; one small reviewed cycle, worker and independent reviewer from different vendors. Settled decisions only (carried from mini-server; records in .clearhead/archive/01a0fb15-b777-75a3-a048-7e0da5722a02.* and charters/services.md): operator dab, UID/GID 1000, in wheel; the desktop's SSH public key authorized for dab; key-only SSH, no root login, no password auth; passwordless sudo scoped to dab; Tailscale installed and tailscaled enabled. Work in the services profile mkosi.profiles/mini-server-arch (built with scripts/mkosi-arch mini-server-arch). The image carries no secrets: the console passphrase (1Password) and Tailscale enrollment happen at install, by Darrion, outside this increment; do not invent a mechanism for either, say in the closing report what install will need. Tests first, in tests/ beside the existing config tests, red before the change. Then build the real image and boot it in a VM with disposable keys, as README's dev-pod VM recipe does, and show from the booted VM: SSH as dab with the test key succeeds, password and root SSH are refused, sudo works for dab without a password, tailscaled is active. If the sandbox cannot boot a VM, stop and report exactly what is missing rather than stubbing the boot. No disk writes outside the build output; no flashing. Short closing report. Orchestrator 2026-11-08: worker blocked, the sandbox has no mkosi, qemu, ssh or pytest, so nothing was built (runs svc-access-11082124, svc-access-2). Retagged +facilitator: the sandbox image needs those tools (or a host-side build route) before this can be dispatched again.$ +facilitator ^2026-11-08T21:23 #01a1bd0b-edf6-74d3-ad29-16117ab97de8
    >[ ] Services image\: RAID1 storage at /srv/storage, optional at boot =services-storage $Second increment of =services-up; brief before dispatch. Settled: the two 4 TB WD USB disks as mdadm RAID1 on GPT partitions, ext4 at /srv/storage, optional at boot, with workloads and backups refusing to run when it is absent. Tested in a VM with virtual disks; the real disks are never written without Darrion's explicit approval. Orchestrator 2026-11-08: no steward here, and this has no dispatchable brief yet (the description says 'brief before dispatch'); it also builds on =services-access, now running as review-cycle svc-access-11082124. Retagged +facilitator to write the brief; retag +orchestrator when briefed.$ +facilitator ^2026-11-08T21:23 <services-access #01a1bd0b-ee03-7023-a189-5f35445a4b94
