[ ] Merge Syncthing conflict copies of plaintext files on the services machine =syncthing-merge $Darrion, 2026-11-04: Syncthing is ClearHead's sync, keeping sync an ops problem with files as the only truth (platform Decision 31's filesystem boundary). Syncthing never merges: the older of two concurrent edits becomes name.sync-conflict-<date>-<device>.ext. A watcher on the always-on N150 only (a second merger could race it) runs git merge-file over the current file, the conflict copy and a base the watcher keeps itself as the last version it saw (not .stversions, which skips local edits). On a clean merge it writes the result and deletes the copy; otherwise it leaves both. Never --union for .actions (it would revive archived lines). Starting point to read, not run blind: https://gist.github.com/Seas0/f4fcd181cc51ab1f1766d7d583bc0cb0 . Acceptance: a three-device test (phone, desktop, server) with offline edits to different actions merging cleanly, and the same action changed on both sides left as a conflict. No ClearHead code.  2026-11-04: once platform =semantic-merge exists, the watcher calls it for .actions files instead of git merge-file, which conflicts on neighbouring lines.$ !3 ^2026-11-04T07:38 <services-up #01a1a57e-d217-7c32-ab1b-e0676fc5dd6f
